blue}0}$ in the ones column. So, we write ${\\color{blue}0}$ below the *ones* and carry ${\\color{red}1}$ to the *tens*:\n\n$$\n1; 1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 9 \\\\ + & 7\\end{vmatrix}1; 0\n$$\n\n**Step 2.** Adding the tens, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}1} + {\\color{blue}1} + {\\color{blue}7} = {\\color{blue}9}{:}\n$$\n\n$$\n1; 1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 9 \\\\ + & 7\\end{vmatrix}1; 9 \\mid 0\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** Adding the hundreds, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}1} + {\\color{blue}0} = {\\color{blue}1}{:}\n$$\n\n$$\n1; 1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 9 \\\\ + & 0\\end{vmatrix}7\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{vmatrix}9 \\mid 0\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n119 + 71 = 190\n$$" "Now, let's calculate the following sum:\n\n$$\n119 + 71\n$$\n\nTo use the standard algorithm, we first line up our numbers (*ones* over *ones*, *tens* over *tens*, *hundreds* over *hundreds*):\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ + & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNext, we proceed by adding the numbers in each place value (from right to left):\n\n**Step 1.** Adding the ones, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}9} + {\\color{blue}1} = {\\color{red}1}{\\color{blue}0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can't write ${\\color{red}1}{\\color{blue}0}$ in the ones column. So, we write ${\\color{blue}0}$ below the *ones* and carry ${\\color{red}1}$ to the *tens*:\n\n$$\n1; 1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 9 \\\\ + & 7\\end{vmatrix}1; 0\n$$\n\n**Step 2.** Adding the tens, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}1} + {\\color{blue}1} + {\\color{blue}7} = {\\color{blue}9}{:}\n$$\n\n$$\n1; 1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 9 \\\\ + & 7\\end{vmatrix}1; 9 \\mid 0\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** Adding the hundreds, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}1} + {\\color{blue}0} = {\\color{blue}1}{:}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{ccccc} &  &  & \\hspace{-0.167em}\\hspace{-0.167em}\\hspace{-0.167em}\\hspace{-0.167em}1\\hspace{-0.167em}\\hspace{-0.167em}\\hspace{-0.167em}\\hspace{-0.167em} &  \\\\  &  & \\hspace{-0.167em}\\hspace{-0.167em}\\hspace{-0.167em}\\hspace{-0.167em}{\\color{blue}{1}}\\hspace{-0.167em}\\hspace{-0.167em}\\hspace{-