iating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to -\\infty $ when $y\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=3y-2$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $-\\infty $ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\infty $ | $-2$ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{8}{(3y-2)^{6}}\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}\\frac{8}{3{u}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}\\frac{8}{3{u}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{8}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-2}{u}^{-6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{5}{u}^{-5}]}_{a}^{-2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{15}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{{u}^{5}}]}_{a}^{-2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{15}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\frac{1}{(-2)^{5}}-\\frac{1}{{a}^{5}}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{15}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{32}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{60}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, we substitute $u=3y-2.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to -\\infty $ when $y\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=3y-2$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $-\\infty $ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\infty $ | $-2$ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{8}{(3y-2)^{6}}\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}\\frac{8}{3{u}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}\\frac{8}{3{u}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{8}{3}\\lim_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-2}{u}^{-6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\li